    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5796\n\nSPONSOR: MURRAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the Ruth AME Zion Church to file with\nthe town of Brookhaven assessor an application for certain real property\ntax exemptions\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the assessor of the Town of Brookhaven to accept an appli-\ncation for real property taxes with respect to the 2020 assessment roll\nfrom Ruth AME Zion Church\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the tax assessor of the town of Brookhaven to\naccept from Ruth AME Zion Church an application for exemption from the\n2020 assessment roll of real property taxes for the property located at\n105 Station Road in Bellport, Town of Brookhaven, county of Suffolk.\nSection 2 establishes an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nExisting law authorizes tax exemptions to be granted after the taxable\nstatus date has passed if after a bill is chaptered authorizing an\nassessor to accept the late application. The Town of Brookhaven Tax\nAssessor has notified the property owner of the need for this legis-\nlation and the willingness to accept an application once a bill is chap-\ntered.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.8727/A.9793 - Referred to Local Government in Senate; Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
